{{Quote|An Imperial Starpath unit was stolen from the Steergard Naval Yard and found at the scene.|[[Dedra Meero]]|<ref name="Aldhani">{{Andor|Aldhani (episode)}}</ref>}}
The '''Steergard Naval Yard''',<ref name="Aldhani" /> also known as the '''Imperial Naval Base''',<ref name="Reckoning" /> was an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[airbase]]<ref name="Aldhani" /> located in [[Steergard]]. At some point, an [[Imperial N-S9 Starpath Unit]] was [[Thief|stolen]] from the base by [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]].<ref name="Reckoning" /> Three sealed targeting deflectors were also stolen by the yard at some point, eventually ending up in [[Luthen Rael]]'s hands.<ref name="N5">{{Andor|Narkina 5 (episode)}}</ref>

{{Struct-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The Imperial Naval Base was first mentioned in an official for the ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' television series, which was released on [[August 24]], [[2022]].<ref name="Andor">{{SWYouTube|N5S9Vx3-QM0|Steal from the Empire &#124; Andor &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/official-clip-andor}}</ref> It was first identified in the subtitles for ''[[Andor: A Disney+ Day Special Look]]'', a documentary about the series.<ref name="Special Look">''[[Andor: A Disney+ Day Special Look]]''</ref>

